  "explain": {
   "text": "A fraction of a fraction is a multiply.[^1] Half of three-quarters: cut every quarter in two, 4 × 2 = 8 equal pieces, and keep one row of the three shaded, 3 × 1 = 3: 3/8.[^2][^3]\n\nOn a 32 A circuit, three-quarters is 24 A; half of that is 12 A, and so is 3/8 of 32 A.\n\nName it too early and 3 of 7 unequal pieces reads 3/7: about 13.7 A, not 12 A.\n\n**Tops times tops, bottoms times bottoms: half of 3/4 is 3/8.**"
  },
  "analogy": {
   "text": "Rating factors multiply: 0.8 for grouping, then 0.9 for temperature, gives 0.72 of the tabled rating, as 8/10 × 9/10 = 72/100.",
   "breaks": "Nothing is cut, so there is no picture to check against; the factors come from tables."
  },
  "practice": {
   "text": "**Rule of thumb:** 'of' means multiply: tops by tops, bottoms by bottoms.\n\n**Worked example:** a 50 m drum has 2/5 left; you need 3/4 of that. 3/4 × 2/5 = 6/20 = 3/10 of the drum: 15 m.\n\n**Common mistakes**\n- Matching pieces first: 2/4 × 3/4 = 6/4.\n- Reading 3 of 7 unequal pieces as 3/7."
  },
